## 🎯 `-sn` (No Port Scan / Host Discovery Only)

```bash
sudo nmap -sn 10.200.6.0/24
```

- `-sn` (formerly `-sP`) tells Nmap: **"Only check if hosts are alive — do NOT scan any ports."**
- If `-sn` is **omitted**, Nmap will discover live hosts **and then automatically run a full port scan** on each one found.
- This makes `-sn` extremely useful for quick network mapping / asset discovery without the noise of a full port scan.

